VERDICT: a const fn does read cfg, so F159-2's premise is verified
         independently of 157's probe and the finding stands on its own
         evidence rather than on 157's.

         One sharpening of F159-2's own wording, from this run. The base
         build's lowered body is 'cmp; csel', which is check-SHAPED. It
         is not a validity check: it is the saturating semantics the type
         declares, which is arithmetic and is what I15 permits. The claim
         F159-2 needs is the narrower one this probe measures: neither
         build branches on the build, and each emits one path. I15's
         property holds in both builds while the denotation differs
         between them, which is a relation no single build can witness.
